# ============================================================================
# SAFETY FIRST — this repo must never carry store-level financial data.
# Once a file is committed, it stays in git history permanently even if
# deleted later, so everything data-shaped is excluded here BEFORE the first
# commit, both by folder name (the real source layout, CLAUDE.md section 4)
# and by file-extension pattern as a second line of defence.
# ============================================================================

# Raw data, database, warehouse and exports — per CLAUDE.md section 4, none
# of this belongs in version control.
data/
db/
warehouse/
exports/
logs/

# The real source folders as handed over (CLAUDE.md section 4) — raw business
# data for 190 stores, never committed, excluded by exact name.
1. POS Sales/
2. Settlement reports/
3. CMS received/
4. Petty cash ledger/
5.CMS DEPOSIT MASTER/
5a. Pickup location master/
6.MID WISE STORE CODE MASTER/
Opening balance at store/
closing balance at store/

# SQLite database and its write-ahead-log companions — explicit patterns as a
# second line of defence beyond the db/ folder rule above (a db file could in
# principle be created elsewhere).
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db

# Every spreadsheet/archive/columnar data format, anywhere in the tree — a
# second line of defence beyond the named folders above. No legitimate code,
# test or doc file in this repo uses any of these extensions.
*.xlsb
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.zip
*.parquet

# Credentials and secrets — never committed, regardless of location.
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*secret*
*credential*
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
